  "content": "Kano Connect - Render Deployment Environment Variables\n=====================================================\n\nThis document lists all environment variables required for the Kano Connect application\ndeployed on Render, along with the APIs and services used in the project.\n\n--- PROJECT OVERVIEW ---\nKano Connect is an enterprise logistics/delivery platform with multi-role dashboards\n(Customer, Rider, Dispatcher, Admin, Super Admin), live GPS tracking over Socket.IO,\nPaystack payments, Cloudinary uploads, Nodemailer emails, Recharts reports, and a PWA.\n\n--- API SERVICES AND INTEGRATIONS ---\n\n1. MONGODB (Database)\n   - Service: MongoDB\n   - Used for: User data, shipments, deliveries, orders, ratings\n   - Connection: MONGODB_URI environment variable\n   - Documentation: https://www.mongodb.com/docs/\n\n2. PAYSTACK (Payments)\n   - Service: Paystack (Africa payment gateway)\n   - Used for: Payment processing, transaction validation, refunds\n   - Keys needed:\n     * PAYSTACK_SECRET_KEY - Server-side secret key\n     * PAYSTACK_PUBLIC_KEY - Frontend public key\n   - Documentation: https://paystack.com/docs\n   - API endpoints:\n     - Initialize transaction: /initialize\n     - Verify transaction: /verify\n     - List transactions: /transaction\n\n3. CLOUDINARY (Media Storage)\n   - Service: Cloudinary\n   - Used for: User avatars, shipment photos, documentation images\n   - Keys needed:\n     * CLOUDINARY_CLOUD_NAME\n     * CLOUDINARY_API_KEY\n     * CLOUDINARY_API_SECRET\n   - Documentation: https://cloudinary.com/documentation\n   - Use case: Image upload, transformation, storage\n\n4. SMTP / EMAIL (Nodemailer)\n   - Service: Any SMTP email server\n   - Used for: User registration, password reset, shipment notifications\n   - Variables needed:\n     * SMTP_HOST (e.g., smtp.gmail.com, smtp.mailtrap.io)\n     * SMTP_PORT (e.g., 587 for TLS, 465 for SSL)\n     * SMTP_USER (email username)\n     * SMTP_PASS (email password or app password)\n   - Documentation: https://nodemailer.com/about/\n\n5. GOOGLE MAPS (Geolocation)\n   - Service: Google Cloud Maps Platform\n   - Used for: Rider location tracking, customer delivery addresses, route planning\n   - Variable: GOOGLE_MAPS_API_KEY\n   - Documentation: https://developers.google.com/maps\n   - Required APIs:\n     - Maps JavaScript API\n     - Geocoding API\n     - Directions API (optional)\n\n6. REDIS (Caching/Queues)\n   - Service: Redis (or Redis-compatible)\n   - Used for: Real-time tracking, session caching, job queues\n   - Variable: REDIS_URL\n   - Documentation: https://redis.io/docs/\n\n7. JWT (Authentication)\n   - Used for: Access token and refresh token generation\n   - Variables:\n     * JWT_SECRET - Sign access tokens\n     * JWT_REFRESH_SECRET - Sign refresh tokens\n   - Library: jsonwebtoken (Node.js)\n\n--- FRONTEND CONFIGURATION ---\n\n8. VITE_API_URL\n   - Used by: Vite build process\n   - Purpose: Configures API base URL for frontend environment\n   - Value example: https://kanoconnect-api.onrender.com\n   - Definition: vite.env.ts or .env file at build time\n\n--- BACKEND CONFIGURATION ---\n\n9. NODE_ENV\n   - Value: production\n   - Purpose: Sets Node.js environment mode\n\n10. PORT\n    - Value: 10000\n    - Purpose: Server listening port (Render sets this automatically)\n\n11. CLIENT_URL\n    - Purpose: Frontend URL for API CORS and redirect URIs\n    - Value example: http://localhost:5173 (dev) or https://kano-web.onrender.com (prod)\n\n--- RENDER DEPLOYMENT ---\n\nrender.yaml Configuration:\n- Service 1: kanoconnect-api (Node.js backend)\n  - Build: cd backend && npm install\n  - Start: cd backend && npm start\n  - Health check: /health\n  - Runtime: node\n\n- Service 2: kanoconnect (Static frontend)\n  - Build: cd frontend && npm install && npm run build\n  - Publish: frontend/dist\n  - Runtime: static\n\n--- SECURITY NOTES ---\n\n- All environment variables marked with sync: false must be set manually in Render Dashboard\n- Never commit .env files or sensitive values to the repository\n- Use Render's \"Environment\" section to add each variable per service\n- Recommended: Use Render's secret management for JWT secrets, Paystack keys, etc.\n\n--- END OF DOCUMENT ---"
